Q: Heic images with filepond A: <p>The core issue is that FilePond's image preview and resize plugins use the browser's native image decoding, which doesn't support HEIC on Chrome or Firefox (only Safari). So the resize plugin fails silently and passes the raw unresized HEIC.</p>
<p>Two solutions:</p>
<p>Option 1 — Client-side (before upload): Add heic2any to convert HEIC to JPG in the browser before FilePond processes it:</p>
<pre><code>import heic2any from 'heic2any';
// intercept the file before addfile event
pond.on('addfile', async (error, file) =&gt; {
  if (file.fileType === 'image/heic') {
    const jpg = await heic2any({ blob: file.file, toType: 'image/jpeg', quality: 0.85 });
    // replace file in pond with converted jpg
  }
});
</code></pre>
<p><strong>Option 2 — Server-side (PHP):</strong> Accept the HEIC as-is and convert with ImageMagick after upload. Requires <code>libheif</code> installed on the server:</p>
<pre><code> $imagick = new Imagick($heic_path);
$imagick-&gt;setImageFormat('jpeg');
$imagick-&gt;writeImage($jpg_path);
</code></pre>
<pre><code></code></pre>
<p>Option 1 also solves your file size issue — converting client-side before upload means you're sending a compressed JPG instead of a 2.75MB HEIC.</p>

Q: Convert from SwiftUI.Font to UIFont A: <p>I am quite late to this but you can now get UIFont in View in iOS 26 by doing:</p>
<pre><code>@available(iOS 26.0, *)
struct YourView: View {
    @Environment(\.font) var font: Font? // nil if no font modifier was applied
    @Environment(\.fontResolutionContext) var fontContext: Font.Context

    var body: some View {
        let uiFont = getUIFont(font: font, context: fontContext)
        Text(&quot;Font family: \(uiFont?.familyName ?? &quot;none&quot;)&quot;)
    }

    private func getUIFont(font: Font?, context: Font.Context) -&gt; UIFont? {
        guard let font = font else {
            return nil
        }
        let ctFont = font.resolve(in: context).ctFont
        return ctFont as UIFont
    }
}
</code></pre>
